WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.655 --> 00:00:03.079
- Dude, have you seen
Making a Murderer yet?

00:00:03.079 --> 00:00:04.115
- I was just about to ask you,

00:00:04.115 --> 00:00:05.873
I binged it last night, it's incredible.

00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:06.877
- So good, right?

00:00:06.877 --> 00:00:07.885
- So good.

00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:09.360
- Has anyone seen Ned?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.196
- Last time I saw him, it was yesterday.

00:00:11.196 --> 00:00:14.262
He was talking to Alaska.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:16.559
(crunching)

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:19.302
- Someone has to find
out what happened to Ned.

00:00:22.162 --> 00:00:27.114
(spooky violin music)

00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:39.942
- [Ricky] He always had
a smile on his face.

00:00:39.942 --> 00:00:41.741
You could really count on a guy like Ned

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.317
to just, like, brighten your day.

00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:49.053
- He loved his job, he loved his wife.

00:00:49.053 --> 00:00:51.144
- To think that someone
could do something like this

00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:54.463
to a guy like that, makes my blood boil.

00:00:54.463 --> 00:00:56.427
- The morning they brought
in Timothy Treadstone,

00:00:56.427 --> 00:00:59.212
it just, it all started to make sense.

00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:01.333
Of course it'd be him.

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:05.015
(guitar music)

00:01:09.241 --> 00:01:12.140
- This ain't the first time
Alaska got himself in trouble.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.138
- Alaska's the kind of guy that, yeah,

00:01:14.138 --> 00:01:16.657
maybe had some shady parts in his past,

00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:18.478
stealing people's lunches,

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.313
unplugging people's computers.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.379
He ain't a saint, but that
don't make him a murderer.

00:01:23.379 --> 00:01:25.235
I've seen Making A Murderer,

00:01:25.235 --> 00:01:28.602
I think I'd know a murderer if I saw one.

00:02:07.857 --> 00:02:09.254
- I know my roommate didn't do it.

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.297
- He was set up, so he
done got the best people

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.896
in the office to represent him.

00:02:14.236 --> 00:02:15.542
- Ya know, they were the first one's

00:02:15.542 --> 00:02:16.753
to finish Making A Murderer,

00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:19.382
so they know it better than anyone.

00:02:19.382 --> 00:02:21.627
(guitar music)

00:02:21.627 --> 00:02:23.020
- How are you?

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.040
- I didn't see them plant the evidence,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.747
no, but given all the misinformation

00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:29.022
and outright slander
surrounding this employee,

00:02:29.022 --> 00:02:31.019
plus my background in legal expertise

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:32.865
having watched Making A Murderer,

00:02:32.865 --> 00:02:34.047
it wouldn't surprise me one bit

00:02:34.047 --> 00:02:35.558
if there was corruption at work here.

00:02:35.558 --> 00:02:38.006
- I promise nothing bad will happen to you

00:02:38.006 --> 00:02:41.061
if you just say, "I shot Ned."

00:02:41.061 --> 00:02:43.382
- I don't think I should do that.

00:02:43.382 --> 00:02:47.179
- "I shot Ned," say it or I will hurt you.

00:02:47.179 --> 00:02:50.389
- I shot Ned.

00:02:50.389 --> 00:02:53.319
Why would you make me say that?

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:54.724
- So his coworkers had the motivation

00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:56.627
to get him fired, and lo and behold,

00:02:56.627 --> 00:02:59.241
you got this Try Guy, this golden goose,

00:02:59.241 --> 00:03:00.958
just been out of thin air,

00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:02.444
and who was the last person to see him?

00:03:02.444 --> 00:03:04.557
Is, aha, Mr. Treadstone.

00:03:04.557 --> 00:03:06.519
Sounds a lot like Making A Murderer to me.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.143
- Has anyone actually
tried contacting Ned?

00:03:09.143 --> 00:03:12.003
Like stopping by his house
or even giving him a call?

00:03:12.003 --> 00:03:15.556
- I don't know.

00:03:15.556 --> 00:03:17.844
(phone ringing)

00:03:17.844 --> 00:03:19.398
- Hey, man, what's up?

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:20.722
- Ned?

00:03:20.722 --> 00:03:22.115
You're alive?

00:03:22.115 --> 00:03:23.496
Where are you?

00:03:23.496 --> 00:03:25.539
- I'm at home, keep this between us,

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:28.082
but I finally started
watching Making A Murderer

00:03:28.082 --> 00:03:30.774
and I'm taking a personal
day to finish it,

00:03:30.774 --> 00:03:33.921
so good, am I right?

00:03:33.921 --> 00:03:35.000
- That's not Ned.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.002
- What do you mean?

00:03:36.002 --> 00:03:37.860
- Would you ever pick up the
phone while binge-watching

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.272
an episode of Making A Murderer?

00:03:39.274 --> 00:03:41.142
- Oh my god.

00:03:41.142 --> 00:03:44.072
(spooky violin music)

